# S14p, guest g (a k10 character: k2 dies on the route's rock slope): the title gives it the room story at game start
# (the owner's card, without flag 505), so its engine lacks 505 as well although its own card has it (the lobby's
# check). It goes through the lobby into stag0101 and steps on matb01, whose hint panel sets 505: new to the room and
# plausible there (stag0101 sets it), merged at once while the owner is present. run.py's "story_saved" times the
# owner's online_story row from this script's "505 set" line (ten seconds at most). On to stag0102: 505 stays.
# (matb01 lies on the west route at 229,-35: the route goes on from there to the exit matz02.)
campaign until stage=stagml11
talk until control,frames>=60
log in the lobby
idle until frames>=300 fail flag:505=1
log 505 not in the lobby
explore mate00 yes until stage=stag0101,control
log in the field
mat matb01 no until flag:505=1
log 505 set
talk until control,frames>=60
route {route:stag0101_west>218,-26}
mat matz02 yes until stage=stag0102,control
log in stag0102
idle until frames>=120 fail flag:505=0
log 505 kept
idle until frames>=60
